-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the localised modular reduction onto the fibre field
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A \subseteq L$ a subring, $k$ a field and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism, and let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$. Inside the Laurent series field $L((q))$ consider the subring $R =$ `modularRing N A`, the subring generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series `jqModC L` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series obtained from the integral numerator series `jNum` by mapping its coefficients into $L$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$) and `jqNModC L N` (its image under `qExpand`, the level-$N$ substitution); all its elements have coefficients in $A$. Write $O =$ `modularLocalized N A red` for the subring of $L((q))$ of those $f$ admitting a presentation $f s = r$ with $r, s \in R$ and $s$ outside the prime ideal `redKer` attached to $\mathrm{red}$ on $R$, and $\pi_0 =$ `modularRedLocHom N A red : O →+* LaurentSeries k` for the ring homomorphism determined by $\pi_0(f) \cdot \mathrm{redRes}(s) = \mathrm{redRes}(r)$ for any such presentation. Assuming $\mathrm{red}$ is surjective, every element $y$ of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, the intermediate field $k\bigl(\,\mathrm{jqModC}\ k,\ \mathrm{jqNModC}\ k\ N\,\bigr)$ of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by the two reduced expansions, is of the form $y = \pi_0(f)$ for some $f \in O$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the reduction of the modular function field of level $N$ at a prime of its coefficient ring: the localised coefficientwise reduction $\pi_0$ maps the presentation ring $O$ onto the function field of the fibre. It is used in the construction of prolongation tuples and models in the place-specialisation part of the development, in particular for producing a finitely spanned order subalgebra and for the norm-reduction statement there.
